\subsection{Simulation results}
\cref{table1} reports ABC$\rightarrow$D, where the test scene D is unseen. UP-VLA achieves an average length of 4.08, the best in the table, against 3.06 for GR-1 (about 33\% higher) and 3.35 for 3D Diffuser Actor. Among VLA-based baselines, RoboFlamingo reaches 2.47, 3D-VLA 0.71 and UP-VLA-RT-2 1.44, so simply fine-tuning a VLM to emit actions does not close the gap. UP-VLA also keeps its lead as the chain gets longer: its fifth-task success is 0.699, versus 0.430 for the GR-1-like UP-VLA-phi-w/o-mmu and 0.412 for 3D Diffuser Actor, although 3D Diffuser Actor has the highest first-task success (0.938 versus 0.928). The UP-VLA-phi-w/o-mmu model, which shares our backbone and prediction objective, reaches 3.13, close to GR-1; the 0.95 gap to UP-VLA therefore comes from adding understanding and the joint action mechanism rather than from the backbone choice (a conclusion limited by the single reproduction we report).

